---
import CtaLink from '../../components/CtaLink.astro';
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import type { FaqItem } from '../../data/faq';
import { product } from '../../data/product';

const faqs: readonly FaqItem[] = [
	{
		question: 'Do you need a software product before you start an AI agency?',
		answer:
			'No. Start with one kind of business and one task that already slips. A small, safe demonstration is enough to learn whether anyone wants the help.',
	},
	{
		question: 'What should the first offer include?',
		answer:
			'A named problem, a draft workflow a person still approves, a simple price, and a clear limit. Do not promise savings or new customers you have not measured.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Where does AI Agency Engine fit this roadmap?',
		answer: `It is one optional look at ${product.vendor}'s local-business method: free preview videos, Murage, and an advertised live class. It is not a required step, and the class syllabus is not published.`,
	},
];

const steps = [
	{
		index: '01',
		icon: 'building' as const,
		title: 'Choose one type of business',
		text: 'Pick a niche you can visit or already understand, such as roofers, clinics, or local services. A narrow list is easier to research than every business on the street.',
	},
	{
		index: '02',
		icon: 'search' as const,
		title: 'Name a real operational gap',
		text: 'Look for work the business already does by hand: unanswered inquiries, estimates with no follow-up, or review requests that never go out.',
	},
	{
		index: '03',
		icon: 'workflow' as const,
		title: 'Test whether AI can help that task',
		text: 'A draft reply or a research note is a fair test. If the workflow needs private data or a regulated decision, stop and say so.',
	},
	{
		index: '04',
		icon: 'assistants' as const,
		title: 'Build a small, safe demonstration',
		text: 'Use sample information or a public website. Keep a person in the loop. Nothing should send, bill, or change a customer record on its own.',
	},
	{
		index: '05',
		icon: 'email' as const,
		title: 'Explain the service and its limits',
		text: 'Say what the demo does, what a person still checks, and what you are not claiming. An owner should be able to repeat the offer.',
	},
	{
		index: '06',
		icon: 'user' as const,
		title: 'Contact a few relevant businesses',
		text: 'Write to people whose public site shows the task you studied. Personal notes beat a blast. <a href="/how-to-get-your-first-ai-agency-client/">The first-client plan</a> covers that outreach.',
	},
	{
		index: '07',
		icon: 'verified' as const,
		title: 'Validate demand before you build more',
		text: 'A conversation, a paid pilot, or a clear no is useful. A large platform is not. Expand only after someone wants the specific help.',
	},
	{
		index: '08',
		icon: 'calendar' as const,
		title: 'Deliver, watch, and adjust',
		text: 'Agree the scope, check the work, and fix what breaks. A retained service is the routine after the first demo, not the first slide.',
	},
];
---

<GuidePage
	title="How to Start an AI Agency: A Beginner Roadmap"
	description="How to start an AI agency: choose a niche, find one real task, build a safe demo, and test demand before you buy a long program."
	label="Start here"
	h1="How to Start an AI Agency: A Practical Beginner's Roadmap"
	crumb="Start an agency"
	path="/how-to-start-an-ai-agency/"
	related={[
		'/how-to-get-your-first-ai-agency-client/',
		'/ai-agency-engine-for-beginners/',
		'/ai-agency-engine-use-cases/',
	]}
	faqs={faqs}
	cta="Explore AI Agency Engine"
	closingTitle="Practice the sequence, then choose a teacher"
	closingText="You can follow these steps with official tool docs and your own notes. If you want Sean Donahoe’s demonstrated local-business path, review the current AI Agency Engine offer and the November 2026 class dates."
	showTopCta={false}
>
	<p class="lede" slot="lede">
		Starting an AI agency is a service business, not a hunt for another tool. You pick a kind of local business, find one task that slips, show a small safe demo, and learn whether an owner will pay. You do not need a platform on day one.
	</p>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>A roadmap you can follow this month</h2>
			<p class="measure">
				The examples below are illustrations, not client results. A roofing office with stalled estimates is a teaching picture. It is not a business this site signed.
			</p>
			<ol class="steps">
				{
					steps.map((step) => (
						<li>
							<span class="step-badge">{step.index}</span>
							<div class="step-body">
								<h3>
									<Icon name={step.icon} />
									{step.title}
								</h3>
								<p set:html={step.text} />
							</div>
						</li>
					))
				}
			</ol>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section band">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>A short checklist</h2>
			<ul class="note-list">
				<li>One niche, not a list of every industry.</li>
				<li>One task you can point to on a public website.</li>
				<li>A demo that cannot send messages or spend money without a person.</li>
				<li>A one-paragraph offer with a limit and a price you can explain.</li>
				<li>Five relevant conversations before you add more software.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Where a training offer can help</h2>
			<p class="measure">
				Some people want a teacher for the selling half of this roadmap. AI Agency Engine, from {product.vendor}, advertises that kind of look: free videos that turn a website into a demo and an email, Murage on your computer, and a live class on {product.schedule.masterclass}. The {product.advertisedEntryPrice.label} seat is separate from the free registration. The daily lessons are not published, so treat the class as an option to inspect, not as a required step.
			</p>
			<p class="measure">
				<a href="/ai-agency-engine-for-beginners/">The beginner guide</a> says who that option may suit. <a href="/ai-agency-engine-use-cases/">Local-business service ideas</a> can help you choose the first task.
			</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<CtaLink>Explore AI Agency Engine</CtaLink>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</GuidePage>
